From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 12:03:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add an independent HDR ITM target option

Let a session configure the panel's inverse-tone-mapping ceiling without using
ENABLE_GAMESCOPE_HDR, which also forces HDR output and ITM on at startup.
Steam can then own the active HDR state through Gamescope runtime properties.
---
 usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
index cc05043..11a8f9d 100755
--- a/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
+++ b/usr/share/gamescope-session-plus/gamescope-session-plus
@@ -237,6 +237,10 @@ if [ -z "$GAMESCOPECMD" ]; then
 		HDR_OPTIONS="$HDR_OPTIONS --hdr-itm-sdr-nits $GAMESCOPE_HDR_NITS --hdr-sdr-content-nits $GAMESCOPE_HDR_NITS"
 	fi
 
+	if [ -n "${GAMESCOPE_HDR_ITM_TARGET_NITS:-}" ] && gamescope_has_option "--hdr-itm-target-nits"; then
+		HDR_OPTIONS="$HDR_OPTIONS --hdr-itm-target-nits $GAMESCOPE_HDR_ITM_TARGET_NITS"
+	fi
+
 	GAMESCOPECMD="$(get_gamescope_binary) \
 		$CURSOR \
 		$RESOLUTION \
-- 
